    "before": "Complete Python Fundamentals. Review sequences, numeric expressions and zero-based indexing. NumPy arrays have explicit shape and dtype contracts that Python lists do not provide.",
    "intro": "A telemetry feed stores small integer values efficiently, but multiplying two readings in the same narrow dtype silently wraps the result. Correct numerical computing includes the intermediate representation, not just the printed final type.",
    "sections": [
