        "heading": "Fixed-width storage has finite range",
        "paragraphs": [
          "NumPy integer dtypes such as int8, int16 and int64 have fixed-width ranges. Use iinfo to inspect integer limits and finfo for floating-point properties. Python integers and NumPy fixed-width arrays do not have identical overflow behavior. A valid input value can still produce an out-of-range intermediate result.",
          "Choose a sufficiently wide dtype before arithmetic that needs it. Casting an already overflowed result to a wider dtype cannot reconstruct the lost value. Converting fractional floating-point values to integers also loses fractional information; make rounding and range requirements explicit rather than treating a cast as a validation step."
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Separate storage efficiency from correctness",
        "paragraphs": [
